WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.200
-I have to get into a lot
of things, but first,

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.801
I want to congratulate you on
recently getting engaged.

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:07.801
-Oh, thanks.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:10.934
-I'm so happy for you.

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:13.234
-Also, knocked it out
of the park, just saying.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:14.334
-You did?
-Yeah.

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:15.767
-Really?
-Yeah. No, I scored.

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:17.167
-It's the best thing
in the world.

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:18.534
I can't even tell you.

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:21.400
Now you have a buddy who kind of
has to do things with you.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.701
-I know, and we have to, like,

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:24.567
help each other out
with stuff, too.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:25.934
-Yeah, it's a whole thing now.

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:28.133
-You got to do the stuff
I don't want to do, man.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:29.534
[ Laughter ]
-That's the way it works.

00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:31.534
It's a relationship, exactly.
-Yeah.

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:33.901
-I love -- You know, every time
you come on the show

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:36.167
and your name comes up,
everyone always says,

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.667
"Man, she's the coolest."

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.901
And I -- Really.
You have a great reputation.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.234
And I just want you to know that
we love you here.

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:44.234
-Dude, I love that.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:47.033
-Yeah, do you feel like
you're cool?

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:49.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:51.334
-Um, well, it's freezing
in here.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:54.868
-Yeah, yeah, I'm talking about
temperature-wise, yeah, yeah.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:58.133
But were you always
the cool kid in school?

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:00.300
-Oh, man, no, I was
so inside out.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.667
Are you kidding?
-Oh, really?

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:04.467
-It's taken years to get to
this conversational point.

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:07.434
-Yeah.
Just like in and just shy?

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:11.300
-Yeah, totally shy, and also,
like, you think about

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.133
the cool kids in school,
usually, it's either like --

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:16.334
now, it's synonymous with nice
now that you're -- as adults.

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:19.834
But as a kid, cool is,
like, usually, like, bullies.

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:21.667
I only ever had
one bully experience.

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.701
I was, like, mean to someone
once, and from then on, was

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.100
like, "Absolutely never again."

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.734
I threw nachos in someone's face
because they were mean to me

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.133
in kindergarten.
-You threw --

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:30.434
-And it had been
years and years, and then,

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:33.868
straight after that, I was,
like, forever changed.

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:35.200
-Really?
-I saw this girl's face change

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.267
and I was like,
"Absolutely not."

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:37.334
That's not -- Yeah. No.
-Wow.

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:39.400
Because she was bullying you
or why?

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.334
-She took my best friend
in kindergarten

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.767
and I was like,
"Honestly, who are you?"

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:45.801
-Yeah, and "Dude, I'm about
to flip this plate of nachos."

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:46.934
-It was so impulsive.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:50.367
It came from a deep-seated
resentment in me.

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:52.067
It was a physical reaction.
She walked by and I was like,

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:53.667
"Ooh, that girl,"
and just went like that.

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:55.934
-Yeah.
-"Who do you think you are?

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.167
Is that funny to you?"

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:58.634
I wasn't -- I didn't think
it was funny.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:00.667
-So it changed your life.
-Yeah, I'm starting to sweat.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:02.434
And it's not hot -- I mean,
it's not cold in here anymore.

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.200
[ Laughter ]
I'm burning alive.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.901
-You came on as cool
and now you're warm.

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.300
This is so interesting.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.901
I'm happy that you got over
that, yeah.

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:12.868
But then, your parents
are in the business.

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:16.334
And so, did they get you
into this gig?

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:17.467
Or do you remember this girl?

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:18.901
She was in --
-This poor child.

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:20.734
-She was in the "Flintstones"
live-action movie.

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:22.467
[ Audience aws ]

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.100
How cute are you?
-Wow.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.100
-Do you remember this?
-I do.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.234
-"Flintstones Viva Rock Vegas."

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:30.067
-Yeah.
-It was your first acting role.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:31.234
-Uh-huh.
-Yeah.

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:32.334
And how did that come about?

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:34.067
Were you just like --
Were you nervous?

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:35.634
-I nailed it on the first take.

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.300
At the time, it was
a serious point of pride.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.000
I was the ring toss girl,
so I had to get this, like,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.734
massive flint stone ring
around a Neanderthal.

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:44.667
And my mom was
the script supervisor,

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:47.701
and I was kicking it around set
and just never wanted to leave.

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.033
And so they were like,
"Give her a job."

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.300
And there I -- There's my start.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.467
-We actually have the clip here.

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:55.267
This is the back of
Kristen Stewart's head

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:57.968
making its very brief
big-screen debut

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:00.567
in "The Flintstones
in Viva Rock Vegas."

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:01.434
-Can't wait.

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:03.534
-Come on.

00:03:03.534 --> 00:03:04.868
-Yay!

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.167
-[ Laughs ]
Dude, that was it.

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:10.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:12.968
Dude, come on, that's the best!

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:14.968
-Also, like, right afterwards --
I know, I go...

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:17.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:19.767
Yeah, it's cool.
-I guess you nailed it.

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:22.367
Yeah, I don't know, man.
Oh, my God.

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:24.100
That is a great first clip.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.334
I love that.

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:27.200
And here we are 21 years later,

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.000
I think or 20 years later,
playing Princess Diana.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.968
Amazing job, by the way.

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:34.400
Everybody, the whole --

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.267
the director, everyone,
did a great job.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:38.667
But you mastered the accent
and everything.

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:42.234
You know, and I love
seeing people

00:03:42.234 --> 00:03:43.868
that are great at what they do.

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:46.567
But watching you act, I just --
I got lost.

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:49.000
I didn't -- I just thought it
was Diana watching for a while.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.100
I'm like,
"This is so fascinating."

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.467
Tough to do the accent, is it?

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.367
-Yeah.
Yeah, it's, like, so muscular.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:56.801
It's exhausting.
You have to like --

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:59.234
When I speak, I feel like
I don't open my mouth

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:01.133
and I feel like this,
like, croaked fr--

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:03.634
Words come out of her mouth
like bubbles.

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.200
And I'm like bricks
to the floor.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.133
-Yeah, right?
I mumble all the time as well.

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:11.267
But I mean, it's just --
it was -- anyways.

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:13.534
You get the call
to play Princess Diana,

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.000
and what's your first thought?

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.701
You go, "Challenging?"

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:18.100
-"Dude, are you sure?"
[ Laughs ]

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.667
-Yeah, right?
-Yeah.

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:21.234
-But why do you --
It feels like, to me,

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:23.033
you put yourself
in these positions sometimes.

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:25.601
Like, I would say "Twilight"
was a big deal because...

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:27.000
[ Woman giggles ]
...you came --

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.000
That book was massive.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.434
-Giggles.
-Yeah, people --

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:30.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.934 --> 00:04:32.434
You were like, "Dude, I don't
want to mess this up.

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:35.634
This is -- a lot of people --
These are serious books, man.

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:37.067
I can't mess this up."
-Yeah.

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:38.834
-And you didn't.
You hit a home run.

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:41.701
You knocked it out of the park.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:41.701 --> 00:04:45.000
And then you get this,
and it's another pressure thing

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.133
and you go, "Ooh, I could easily
just not take these roles."

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:49.734
-Yeah.
-And you can just skate on by,

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:51.534
and go, "Yeah, yeah."
But it's a challenge.

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:53.501
I love that you took it.
-Yeah.

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:55.334
Gosh, I mean, like, you know,
I've been doing this

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:57.667
for a minute, so there's
really no way to --

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:59.934
there's no reason to keep going
unless you're going to try and,

00:04:59.934 --> 00:05:02.501
you know, push the envelope,
and...

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:08.467
Also, like, if you cancel out
all of that noise, she's so...

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:11.767
She's so sparkly
and she's, like, so completely

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:13.400
complicated and difficult
to understand.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.334
And we lost this person
too early.

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:17.634
And so I think that we're always
kind of -- we're never going to

00:05:17.634 --> 00:05:19.501
have the information
that we want to have.

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:20.834
-No.
-So I was like,

00:05:20.834 --> 00:05:25.100
"Just embed yourself in your own
desires and curiosities

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.033
and try and sort of not think
about other people's."

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:30.200
But I will say that the weight
of that matters.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.200
Her connection to people
matters. That's who she was.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.000
Like, the reason we're telling
this story still

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.501
is because she just, like...
-Yeah.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.300
-She reached out and touched
people in a way that

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:40.300
nobody ever really has,
especially in that environment.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.200
So, yeah.
-I want to show --

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.667
You did a fantastic job.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:46.667
Here's Kristen Stewart
in "Spencer."

00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:48.234
Take a look.

00:05:48.234 --> 00:05:54.033
-Mummy, why do we have to open
our presents on Christmas Eve?

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:57.067
Why not Christmas Day
like everybody else?

00:05:57.067 --> 00:05:58.901
-You know at school,
you do tenses?

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:00.300
-Yeah.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:02.767
-It's past, the present, future.

00:06:02.767 --> 00:06:04.367
-Right.

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:07.000
-Well, here, there is
only one tense.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.367
There is no future.

00:06:09.367 --> 00:06:11.901
The past and the present
are the same thing.

00:06:11.901 --> 00:06:15.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:15.434 --> 00:06:17.200
-It's getting
a little Oscar buzz,

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.968
and it should, for good reason.

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:20.267
Kristen Stewart, everybody!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.267 --> 00:06:23.801
"Spencer" is in theaters
nationwide on Friday.

